<title>USA: Intl Flavors says strong dollar hurt sales.</title>
<headline>Intl Flavors says strong dollar hurt sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Flavors &amp; Fragrances Inc said the stronger U.S. dollar eroded its sales gains in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>IFF said its worldwide sales would have risen about five percent over the first quarter of last year if the dollar exchange rate had stayed the same.</p>
<p>Sales at IFF were essentially flat at $382.8 million in the quarter versus $382.8 million a year ago.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
